== P0 sanity: valid streams (harness proof) ==
anthropic valid stream      -> Known(in=Some(25), out=Some(9), provenance=Reported)
google valid stream         -> Known(in=Some(88), out=Some(19), provenance=Reported)

== P1 anthropic streaming, contract-violating usage fragments ==
anthropic stream negative output_tokens     -> Invalid(usage field /usage/output_tokens is negative (-5): a token count is never negative; the fact is marked invalid, never saturated)
anthropic stream float output_tokens        -> Invalid(usage field /usage/output_tokens is a non-integer number (1.5): a token count is an integer; the fact is marked invalid, never rounded)
anthropic stream string output_tokens       -> Invalid(usage field /usage/output_tokens is not a JSON number (string): a token count is never a string or container)
anthropic stream negative input half   -> Invalid(usage field /usage/input_tokens is negative (-3): a token count is never negative; the fact is marked invalid, never saturated)

== P2 google streaming, contract-violating usageMetadata ==
google stream negative candidatesTokenCount   -> Invalid(usage field /usageMetadata/candidatesTokenCount is negative (-7): a token count is never negative; the fact is marked invalid, never saturated)
google stream float promptTokenCount          -> Invalid(usage field /usageMetadata/promptTokenCount is a non-integer number (8.5): a token count is an integer; the fact is marked invalid, never rounded)
google stream string candidatesTokenCount     -> Invalid(usage field /usageMetadata/candidatesTokenCount is not a JSON number (string): a token count is never a string or container)

== P3 openai-completions streaming (control): same violations ==
openai stream negative prompt_tokens     -> Invalid(usage field /usage/prompt_tokens is negative (-3): a token count is never negative; the fact is marked invalid, never saturated)
openai stream float completion_tokens    -> Invalid(usage field /usage/completion_tokens is a non-integer number (5.5): a token count is an integer; the fact is marked invalid, never rounded)

== P4 anthropic mixed: invalid fragment AFTER a valid one ==
anthropic stream valid-then-invalid delta -> Invalid(usage field /usage/output_tokens is negative (-4): a token count is never negative; the fact is marked invalid, never saturated)

== P5 Estimated-state ledger round-trip (doc §10 claims coverage) ==
estimated round-trip -> usage_state preserved: true (basis Some(Estimated { basis: "probe-basis" }))

== P6 FinalSnapshot fold: identical numbers, different provenance ==
FinalSnapshot fold reported-then-estimated same numbers -> Err("two different final usage snapshots for one request ((Some(10), Some(3)) then (Some(10), Some(3))): a conflict is never merged")
